{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwbD9T86wjsdVBEu6W3d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard to check the charts render, and the rule's status is still \"pending\" because it hasn't run yet.\n\n**What the data holds:** `kibana_sample_data_logs` is web access logs, with `timestamp` as the time field. The fields that matter most:\n- **Traffic:** `response` (a string status code, so I used `response.keyword`), `bytes`, `extension`, `request`, `url`.\n- **Client and geography:** `clientip`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `agent`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-446e33cc Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests (single number)\n- Requests over time (line chart)\n- Responses by status code (pie chart)\n- Bytes by file extension (bar chart)\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-446e33cc-web-logs-overview-1bf79c902200.\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-446e33cc 5xx spike\" (id `32090337-119e-46a8-b0c6-402d577fe5ac`) checks every minute. It matches documents whose `response.keyword` is a 5xx code and fires when there are more than 10 in the last 5 minutes. It has no actions attached, so when it fires it will only show as an alert in Kibana."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1175,"cache_read_input_tokens":19741,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1175},"output_tokens":466,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"65839f47-39c7-4cd7-9c84-86ca242b09e5","timestamp":"2026-10-12T02:56:09.494Z","request_id":"req_011CfwbD9GCgFLSWEsAgEmMj"}
